{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-convo/src/derive.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:42:33.382654Z","id":"7d9edc9413f65e80cf8c16ac5ad24a5bb643f2645c43cf78dd465af37c591c1e","body":{"detail":"Found drawing document@claude-session in toolpath.net's visualizer (2026-10-19): attachment events parented to the first user turn formed a side chain that took the head (steps.last()), so every assistant turn sat outside ancestors(head). Test: test_head_stays_on_the_conversation_when_events_branch_off_an_earlier_turn; claude and claude-session documents now head at claude-preamble-8, the tip after the last turn.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":427},"content_hash":"af1349b9f5f9a1a6a0404dea36dcc9499bcb25c9adc112b7cc9a93cae41f3262"},"summary":"path.head is the latest step whose ancestry holds the last turn: an event side chain off an earlier turn no longer takes the head and turns the conversation into a dead end","tags":["goldens","dead-end","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
